{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T11:43:16.684Z","data":{"text":"Done. Task 2 is complete.\n\nSummary of what I implemented:\n\n- **Port**: `vcs.ts` now exports `VcsPushResult` and adds `fetchBranch`/`pushBranch` to `Vcs`.\n- **Remote module** (`git-vcs-remote.ts`): exact `git fetch --no-tags <remote> refs/heads/<branch>` + `FETCH_HEAD` read, and `git push --porcelain <remote> <commit>:refs/heads/<branch>` (no `+`, no force). Both use `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, return git's combined output, map a porcelain `!` `[rejected]` line to `{ status: 'rejected' }`, and throw otherwise.\n- **Wiring**: `GitVcs` delegates through a remote context bounded by `timeouts.gitRemoteSeconds` (default `DEFAULT_GIT_REMOTE_SECONDS = 120` in `config-vcs.ts`; `OsqTimeouts` gained the optional key, `DEFAULT_CONFIG` unchanged). `NoVcs` rejects both.\n- **Tests**: `vcs-write.test.ts` updated (port members, forbidden args, new push-containment case); new `tests/vcs-remote.test.ts` covers every \"Vcs remote operations\" scenario against a bare `origin` plus two clones, and `NoVcs`.\n\nBoth the task verify (`tests/vcs-remote.test.ts`, 5 passing) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass. Result written to `openspec/changes/161-osq-server/.run/results/2.md`."}}
